Solder Bop
Ingredients: SOUL JAZZ / JAZZ-FUNK + CYBERPUNK & DYSTOPIAN + Cowbell
Creative Catalyst: Cloistered ascetics at an alpine relay transcribe nocturnal REM spikes into modular synth control voltages, which subterranean club bands hijack into grease-slick street grooves.

Solder Bop is a grime-caked, tube-saturated collision where greasy Jimmy Smith Hammond organ runs, pocket-heavy funk clavinet, and syncopated Latin-funk cowbell rattle violently against dystopian modular drone spikes, sub-bass seismic rumbles, and industrial decay.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 96–112 BPM; deep, behind-the-beat jazz-funk swing locked into an uncompromising, dry metallic cowbell ostinato, disrupted by sudden rhythmic gate-stutters.
- Harmonic Palette: Minor pentatonic blues cuts and greasy Dorian/Mixolydian chord extensions lacerated by cold diminished intervals, pitch-drifting modular oscillators, and oppressive sub-bass drones.
- Production Signatures: Overdriven rotary speaker cabinets cranked until the tubes squeal; close-mic'd, un-damped raw steel cowbell slicing through low-pass filters; heavy analog tape compression capturing claustrophobic industrial room ambience.
- Dynamics: Brooding, low-lit Rhodes and bass vamps that steadily ratchet tension through relentless percussion layering, finally detonating into howling brass stabs and distorted synth sweeps.

Scene & Origin Lore
In the subterranean canal tunnels beneath the high-altitude Karas Hermitage, decommissioned pumping stations have morphed into illegal dance dives known as "Smelt Rooms." Patrons in oilskin trench coats, protective welding goggles, and velvet-trimmed lapels pack these damp caverns to hear rogue church organists trade licks with modular circuit-hackers. The music was born when renegade technicians leaked cassette tapes of the hermits’ nocturnal brainwave-to-voltage transcriptions into the hands of dockland jazz combos. Rather than treat the jagged synthetic voltages as sacred meditation, these rhythm sections strapped them directly to screaming Hammond organs and battered hand-held cowbells, transforming cloistered insomnia into sweat-drenched, syncopated defiance against a suffocating corporate surface world.

Typical Instruments
- Percussion: Hand-hammered heavy steel cowbell (played with thick wooden dowels), vintage 1970s funk drum kit with deadened snare and punchy kick.
- Keyboards & Organs: Hammond B3 organ with cracked Leslie horn baffles, Hohner Clavinet D6 run through high-gain distortion and envelope filters, Fender Rhodes electric piano.
- Synthesizers: Custom Eurorack modular rigs running random stepped voltages, Buchla-style wavefolders, and resonant low-pass gates.
- Rhythm Section: Fender Jazz Bass (fretless, treated with fuzz octavers) and a tight two-piece brass section (muted trumpet and tenor sax) running through tape delays.

For Fans Of: The Headhunters, The Comet Is Coming, Miles Davis (Dark Magus era), Sons of Kemet

